WEBVTT

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:20.019
( all laughing )

00:00:20.061 --> 00:00:21.521
What’s so funny?

00:00:21.562 --> 00:00:24.649
I think it’s from all
those doggone cocoa beans.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:26.651
Hey, by the way,
did you guys know

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:29.195
that chocolate
contains a property

00:00:29.237 --> 00:00:31.406
that triggers the
release of endorphins?

00:00:31.489 --> 00:00:34.075
Gives one the feeling
of being in love.

00:00:34.158 --> 00:00:36.286
You don’t say.

00:00:37.787 --> 00:00:41.541
All aboard.

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:52.719
Onward.

00:01:02.186 --> 00:01:04.814
( deep, ominous melody resumes )

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:16.868
WONKA:
Here...

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:19.620
Try some of this.
It’ll do you good.

00:01:19.704 --> 00:01:22.540
You look starved
to death.

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:24.876
It’s great!

00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:28.087
That’s because it’s mixed
by waterfall.

00:01:28.171 --> 00:01:30.423
The waterfall
is most important.

00:01:30.506 --> 00:01:31.758
It mixes the
chocolate,

00:01:31.841 --> 00:01:32.675
churns it up,

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:34.719
makes it light
and frothy.

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:38.348
Uh, by the way, no other factory
in the world m...

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:39.682
You already said that.

00:01:42.518 --> 00:01:43.978
( glove squeaking )

00:01:44.062 --> 00:01:46.647
You’re all quite short,
aren’t you?

00:01:46.731 --> 00:01:48.483
Well, yeah.
We’re children.

00:01:48.566 --> 00:01:51.402
Well, that’s no excuse.
I was never as short as you.

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:52.779
You were once.

00:01:52.862 --> 00:01:54.697
Was not! Know why?

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:58.659
Because I distinctly remember
putting a hat on top of my head.

00:01:58.743 --> 00:02:00.453
Look at your short
little arms.

00:02:00.536 --> 00:02:02.955
You could never reach.
( haughty giggle )

00:02:04.957 --> 00:02:07.794
Do you even remember
what it was like being a kid?

00:02:07.835 --> 00:02:10.546
Oh, boy, do I.

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:14.300
Do I?

00:02:14.384 --> 00:02:15.885
NARRATOR:
In fact, Willy Wonka

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:19.472
hadn’t thought
about his childhood for years.

00:02:19.514 --> 00:02:21.599
KIDS:
Trick or treat!

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:23.851
( laughter )

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:30.483
( knocking )

00:02:32.276 --> 00:02:34.028
ALL:
Trick or treat!

00:02:34.112 --> 00:02:35.988
( laughing )

00:02:36.072 --> 00:02:37.281
Who do we have here?

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:39.117
Ruthie, Veronica,

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:43.121
Terrence... and who’s that
under the sheet?

00:02:44.622 --> 00:02:47.291
Little Willy Wonka.

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:48.334
( giggles ):
Oh...

00:02:48.418 --> 00:02:50.795
( wind whistling )

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:52.171
NARRATOR:
Willy Wonka was the son

00:02:52.255 --> 00:02:54.966
of the city’s
most famous dentist--

00:02:55.007 --> 00:02:58.636
Wilbur Wonka.

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:00.763
( door creaking open )

00:03:03.266 --> 00:03:04.350
( door closing )

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:05.977
Now,

00:03:06.018 --> 00:03:09.522
let’s see what the damage is
this year, shall we?

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:14.152
( clattering )

00:03:22.952 --> 00:03:25.037
Caramels.

00:03:25.121 --> 00:03:27.748
They’d get stuck
in your braces, wouldn’t they?

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:35.381
Lollipops.

00:03:35.423 --> 00:03:38.885
What we call
"cavities on a stick."

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:41.137
Then we have all

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.931
this... all this...

00:03:44.015 --> 00:03:46.559
chocolate.

00:03:47.435 --> 00:03:49.061
You know, just last

00:03:49.145 --> 00:03:50.104
week, I was reading,

00:03:50.188 --> 00:03:51.981
in a very important
medical journal, that

00:03:52.064 --> 00:03:54.066
some children are

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:56.402
allergic to chocolate.

00:03:56.486 --> 00:03:59.572
Makes their noses itch.

00:03:59.614 --> 00:04:02.283
Maybe I’m not allergic.

00:04:02.366 --> 00:04:04.076
I could try a piece.

00:04:04.118 --> 00:04:05.620
Really?

00:04:05.703 --> 00:04:07.914
But why take a chance?

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:20.676
( flames whooshing )

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:24.680
CHARLIE:
Mr. Wonka?

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:26.599
Mr. Wonka,
we’re headed

00:04:26.641 --> 00:04:27.892
for a tunnel!

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:29.060
Oh, yeah.

00:04:29.101 --> 00:04:30.895
Uh, full speed ahead.

00:04:37.068 --> 00:04:39.195
How can they see
where they’re going?

00:04:39.278 --> 00:04:40.530
They can’t.

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:42.615
There’s no knowing
where they’re going.

00:04:42.657 --> 00:04:44.575
Switch on the lights.

00:04:53.209 --> 00:04:56.128
♪ ♪

00:05:04.554 --> 00:05:07.306
♪ ♪

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:13.271
People, keep an eye out.

00:05:13.312 --> 00:05:16.816
We’re passing
some very important rooms here.

00:05:21.112 --> 00:05:23.072
What do you use
hair cream for?

00:05:23.155 --> 00:05:24.365
To lock in moisture.

00:05:24.448 --> 00:05:25.950
( laughs )

00:05:28.995 --> 00:05:31.289
( mooing, whips cracking )

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:33.749
Whipped cream.

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:36.002
Precisely. ( giggles )

00:05:36.043 --> 00:05:37.378
That doesn’t make sense.

00:05:37.461 --> 00:05:40.172
For your information,
little girl,

00:05:40.214 --> 00:05:41.173
whipped cream isn’t

00:05:41.257 --> 00:05:42.174
whipped cream at all

00:05:42.258 --> 00:05:43.759
unless it’s been whipped
with whips.

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:46.762
Everybody knows that.

